  "sourceFacts": {
    "horizontalBasis": "Retained Q1519733 / way495122358 anchor [46.301051853,38.073555312] and heading 1.28106383853 rad remain unchanged. Current main feature35184867211190 has30 outer vertices; separate main/rear dome parts35184836590170/171 each have19. The current named Blue Mosque POI agrees. Positive X faces north-northeast toward the entrance: the wide front and rounded corner stumps are at positive X, the narrow chamfered rear annex at negative X; this matches the inspected northern entrance picture. Positive Z runs east-southeast. The two dome plans are retained exactly. Portal, short corner stumps, side cupolas, facade fields and entry steps use picture-led estimates within the main footprint/recess. Azerbaijan Museum, bazaar, park, forecourt and other buildings stay host content.",
    "architecturalHeights": "Current map tags are retained verbatim: main height5 m; main dome min_height5/height10 m; smaller rear dome height7 m. There are no retained independent height facts. These low totals disagree with the two pictured roof/portal proportions. For this explicitly approximate visualization, the wall eaves are8 m, main drum to9.8 m/main dome to18 m, rear dome to11.5 m, entrance portal crest15.4 m and short corner stump tops10 m. This overrides the unqualified map totals; it does not reinterpret them as measured stages. Side roof cupolas reach10.2 m and the entrance steps rise.7 m. All these vertical dimensions and profiles are estimates from pictures and footprint scale, not surveyed or published dimensions. No historic full-height minarets are restored."
